      "writtenOn": "2020-07-03T00:10:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The dependency chain is currently from the direct source module to the prebuilt module, yes. But I think this logic is more natural - if a prebuilt module were to be referenced directly but is marked to not be used, then the \"don\u0027t use\" flag shouldn\u0027t be ignored, right?\n\n\u003e Also, I would like to know when this condition hits. Do you have a specific example?\n\nWith https://android.git.corp.google.com/platform/prebuilts/runtime/+/refs/heads/master/mainline/runtime/sdk/Android.bp in the tree there are errors due to the dependency from source to prebuilt:\n\n```\nerror: bionic/apex/Android.bp:17:1: module \"com.android.runtime\" variant \"android_common_com.android.runtime_image\": \"prebuilt_libdl_android{os:android,image:,arch:arm64_armv8-a_cortex-a73,sdk:,link:static,version:,apex:com.android.runtime}\" required by \"libdl_android\" is a native library providing stub. It shouldn\u0027t be included in this APEX via static linking. Dependency path: com.android.runtime{os:android,arch:commo\nn,apex:com.android.runtime,apex_flattened:image}\n           via tag apex.dependencyTag{name:\"sharedLib\", payload:true}\n    -\u003e libc{os:android,image:,arch:arm64_armv8-a_cortex-a73,sdk:,link:shared,version:,apex:com.android.runtime}\n           via tag cc.DependencyTag{Name:\"static variant\", Library:false, Shared:false, ReexportFlags:false, ExplicitlyVersioned:false, FromStatic:false}\n    -\u003e libc{os:android,image:,arch:arm64_armv8-a_cortex-a73,sdk:,link:static,version:,apex:com.android.runtime}\n           via tag cc.DependencyTag{Name:\"static\", Library:true, Shared:false, ReexportFlags:false, ExplicitlyVersioned:false, FromStatic:false}\n    -\u003e libdl_android{os:android,image:,arch:arm64_armv8-a_cortex-a73,sdk:,link:static,version:,apex:com.android.runtime}\n           via tag android.prebuiltDependencyTag{}\n    -\u003e prebuilt_libdl_android{os:android,image:,arch:arm64_armv8-a_cortex-a73,sdk:,link:static,version:,apex:com.android.runtime}\n```\n\n(I have to patch around another issue to get this far - https://r.android.com/1354624.)",
